From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:07:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: don't wake the NVKMS worker for unneeded non-stall
 interrupts

NVKMS registers for every GPU non-stall interrupt (NV01_EVENT_NONSTALL_INTR
on the subdevice). Those come with every semaphore release that asks for
one, which includes the fences of all GPU clients, and for each one
NonStallInterruptCallback() allocates a timer that runs
nvKmsServiceNonStallInterrupt() on the NVKMS kthread with the global
nvkms_lock held. That function only services deferred request FIFOs
(NVKMS_IOCTL_REGISTER_DEFERRED_REQUEST_FIFO, used by X11 swap groups) and
pending headSurface viewport flips. On a Wayland desktop neither exists,
so all of it is wasted: a GFP_ATOMIC allocation, a kthread wakeup and an
nvkms_lock acquisition per interrupt, about one per frame of every GL
client. On an RTX 4080 Laptop that was 10.9k/s with glmark2-wayland, and
with a video playing on the desktop 418/s, 27 % of the NVKMS kthread's
1543 nvkms_lock acquisitions per second. NVIDIA's own XXX comment in the
callback asks for a lighter-weight check.

Count the deferred request FIFOs and headSurface channels of all devices
in nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount, changed with nvkms_lock held where they
are registered/unregistered and installed into/removed from
pDispEvo->pHsChannel[], and return early from the callback while it is
zero. The callback can't take nvkms_lock (it runs within RM's locks and
can't dereference the device's ref_ptr without it), so it reads the
counter without a lock. That's enough: the count goes up before the
client gets the FIFO handle and before headSurface renders, so the
interrupts they cause see it non-zero. Teardown paths that don't decrement
it only make the callback queue work as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h          |  8 ++++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-headsurface-config.c |  4 ++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c                 | 12 ++++++++++++
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-surface.c            |  6 ++++++
 4 files changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
index e6464c85..25d57743 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/include/nvkms-types.h
@@ -2996,6 +2996,14 @@ typedef struct {
 #endif
 
     struct NvKmsPerOpen *nvKmsPerOpen;
+
+    /*
+     * Number of deferred request FIFOs and headSurface channels, on all
+     * devices: the things nvKmsServiceNonStallInterrupt() services. Changed
+     * with the global NVKMS lock held; NonStallInterruptCallback() reads it
+     * without the lock.
+     */
+    NvU32 nonStallWorkCount;
 } NVEvoGlobal;
 
 extern NVEvoGlobal nvEvoGlobal;
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-headsurface-config.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-headsurface-config.c
index 341c6417..7cef51d2 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-headsurface-config.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-headsurface-config.c
@@ -2284,6 +2284,8 @@ void nvHsConfigStart(
                 (pHsConfigOneHead->pHsChannel == NULL)) {
                 nvHsFreeChannel(pDispEvo->pHsChannel[apiHead]);
                 pDispEvo->pHsChannel[apiHead] = NULL;
+                nvAssert(nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount > 0);
+                nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount--;
                 continue;
             }
 
@@ -2294,6 +2296,8 @@ void nvHsConfigStart(
             nvAssert(pDispEvo->pHsChannel[apiHead] == NULL);
             pDispEvo->pHsChannel[apiHead] = pHsConfigOneHead->pHsChannel;
             pHsConfigOneHead->pHsChannel = NULL;
+            /* See NonStallInterruptCallback(). */
+            nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount++;
         }
     }
 
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c
index 83e4b91e..62b80ea2 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-rm.c
@@ -4321,7 +4321,19 @@ static void NonStallInterruptCallback(
      * XXX It might be nice to use a lighter-weight lock here to check if any
      * requests are pending in any NvKmsDeferredRequestFifo before scheduling
      * nvKmsServiceNonStallInterrupt().
+     *
+     * Non-stall interrupts come with every semaphore release that requests
+     * one, e.g. for each fence of every GPU client, so this would wake the
+     * NVKMS worker and take the nvkms_lock for each of them (thousands per
+     * second under load). nvKmsServiceNonStallInterrupt() only services
+     * deferred request FIFOs and headSurface channels; skip it while none
+     * exist. The count is read without the lock: it changes with the lock
+     * held, before the client can use a new FIFO or headSurface renders, so
+     * any interrupt they cause sees it non-zero.
      */
+    if (*(volatile const NvU32 *)&nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
 
     (void) nvkms_alloc_timer_with_ref_ptr(
         nvKmsServiceNonStallInterrupt, /* callback */
diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-surface.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-surface.c
index bc347e97..9a744a73 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-surface.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/nvkms-surface.c
@@ -1674,6 +1674,9 @@ NVDeferredRequestFifoRec *nvEvoRegisterDeferredRequestFifo(
 
     nvEvoIncrementSurfaceRefCnts(pSurfaceEvo);
 
+    /* Non-stall interrupts need servicing now; see NonStallInterruptCallback(). */
+    nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount++;
+
     return pDeferredRequestFifo;
 }
 
@@ -1687,6 +1690,9 @@ void nvEvoUnregisterDeferredRequestFifo(
     nvAssert(pDeferredRequestFifo->fifo != NULL);
     nvAssert(pDeferredRequestFifo->pSurfaceEvo != NULL);
 
+    nvAssert(nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount > 0);
+    nvEvoGlobal.nonStallWorkCount--;
+
     nvHsLeaveSwapGroup(pDevEvo, pDeferredRequestFifo, FALSE /* teardown */);
 
     nvRmApiUnmapMemory(
